{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>For you shall not go out in haste.</b> As you went out of Egypt." "<b>For He who goes before you.</b> The glory of HaShem." "And the meaning of <b>your rear guard</b> [מאספכם]: because they are scattered in exile. And in my opinion, HaShem will surround them, for the glory goes before them and behind them, like \"the rear guard of all the camps\" (Numbers 10:25)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:12.121403635Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}